            "text": "{\n  \"relation\": \"REFINED\",\n  \"consensus_summary\": \"The firmament is primarily understood as the expanse or vault of the sky that declares God's glory, structurally serving as the boundary that separates the upper waters from the lower waters or the earthly realm from the divine realm.\",\n  \"book_summary\": \"The firmament is the divider separating the gathered heavenly waters above from the restless sea of peoples below, and serves as the place where the ruling lights are set.\",\n  \"consensus_core_identification\": \"A cosmic boundary dividing upper and lower realms/waters, and a visible testament to God's glory.\",\n  \"book_core_identification\": \"A divider between the heavenly waters above and the restless sea of peoples below, containing the ruling lights.\",\n  \"core_relation\": \"COMPATIBLE_OVERLAP\",\n  \"extension_relation\": \"PARTIAL_RECLASSIFICATION\",\n  \"boundary_disagreement\": \"The book preserves the consensus structural definition of the firmament (dividing waters, holding lights) but symbolically specifies the 'waters below' as the 'restless sea of peoples' rather than merely the physical seas or the generic earthly realm.\",\n  \"material_contradiction\": \"There is no direct contradiction of the firmament's function; the divergence lies in the book's specific typological mapping of the lower waters to 'peoples', which the consensus does not feature.\",\n  \"rationale\": \"The book utilizes the standard functional definition of the firmament agreed upon by the consensus (separating waters, holding lights from Genesis 1). It refines this by cross-applying Revelation 17:15 to symbolically define the earthly waters below the firmament as 'peoples', resulting in a more specific, composite symbol.\",\n  \"citation_support\": \"STRONG\",\n  \"strongest_objection\": \"Applying the apocalyptic definition of 'waters' as peoples from Revelation 17:15 to the cosmological 'waters below' in Genesis 1 conflates distinct biblical images, potentially reading later apocalyptic symbolism into foundational cosmological structures.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\"\n}",
